From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 05:14:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: m4: keep the panel EDID path off an
 external T8132 DCP

iomfb_m4_panel_edid() builds the internal panel's EDID (P3 description,
the HDR block with appledrm.panel_edr), reads the panel's ADT values
(peak, potential headroom, bright-surroundings maximum) and offers VRR
with appledrm.panel_vrr_min_hz. On a15y the T8132 backend served only the
internal DCP. Since the sync to Aurora 50d5865ea6 the same backend also
drives the external T8132 DCP (apple,t8132-dcpext), whose sink has its
own EDID: return before any of that for an external DCP, so none of the
J604 panel values can reach an external output, whichever way its
connector is probed.

No change on the internal panel. External DCPs are not enabled on the
J604 (no apple,t8132-dcpext node), so this is a guard for when they are.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
(cherry picked from commit 87e5e1488774c54834601a3854097a052cf75d4b)
(cherry picked from commit fbebb223def753a10ab90d40d1dcc37d6a20a329)
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
index 6e7ffdd48c..01eeb786cb 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
@@ -3142,10 +3142,11 @@ int iomfb_m4_panel_edid(struct apple_dcp *owner, struct drm_connector *connector
 	struct drm_display_mode mode;
 	int ret;
 
-	if (!dcp)
+	/* The internal panel only: an external T8132 output has a sink EDID. */
+	if (!dcp || dcp->external)
 		return 0;
 	/* panel_vrr_min_hz: the compositor may ask for VRR (testing). */
-	if (!dcp->external && READ_ONCE(panel_vrr_min_hz))
+	if (READ_ONCE(panel_vrr_min_hz))
 		drm_connector_set_vrr_capable_property(connector, true);
 	if (!dcp_m4_pf->model_year)
 		return 0;
